SWEET WLAN msgbuf bring-up (patch 0159, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step W7, docs/research/51), boot-arg level sweetwlan=8 = level 7 (patch 0150) + run F,
rows W18..W25: after the firmware is up, check the shared area and ring_info (reads only), store host_cap, the five common ring entries and their indices,
the scratch and ring-update buffers (all addresses inside one 256 KiB wired, contiguous, never-freed host pool), set PCI Bus Master on the endpoint, ring the
host-ready doorbell, and do two WLC_GET_VAR round trips (cur_etheraddr, ver) through the H2D control-submit / D2H control-complete rings, polled. Then check
the pool's guard gaps and clear Bus Master. Bus Master is also cleared first by the restore of every stop. Ring indices stay in chip RAM (no host index
buffer). No interrupt mask, S2MPU, SysMMU or inbound iATU write. Levels 1..7 are unchanged: the run F tuples are visible to the writer only at level 8
(swl_wr_pick), and the glue's new gates (EP Command, the two PCIe core doorbells, a bounded number of chip-RAM stores after the release) need level 8.
